WEBVTT

00:03:28.996 --> 00:03:32.621
is one of the primary signals
of nutrient deficiency.

00:03:33.663 --> 00:03:36.829
Assuming that we are getting
glucose regularly,

00:03:36.871 --> 00:03:41.704
how does the specific type
of carbohydrates we eat affect our brains?

00:03:41.746 --> 00:03:43.996
Carbs come in three forms:

00:03:44.038 --> 00:03:46.413
starch, sugar, and fiber.

00:03:46.954 --> 00:03:49.329
While on most nutrition labels,

00:03:49.371 --> 00:03:53.038
they are all lumped
into one total carb count,

00:03:53.079 --> 00:03:56.079
the ratio of the sugar and fiber subgroups
to the whole amount

00:03:56.121 --> 00:03:59.454
affects how the body and brain respond.

00:03:59.496 --> 00:04:02.704
A high glycemic food, such as white bread,